{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518021220,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MzgyNzU2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363827560"},"message":"Thanks @joeyh for heads up.  I am not sure why should it crash -- if annex sends some command which we have no support (`req_` method), then `getattr` returns None and we send `UNSUPPORTED-REQUEST` to annex, so we should be ok.\n\nBut I am still wondering why not to maintain compatibility by relying on special remotes requesting specific version/features support, like I have outlined in http://git-annex.branchable.com/design/exporting_trees_to_special_remotes/#comment-b3876cc7b791c6b8cb12949bdbbf8268\n\nThat would preclude braking compatibility with any existing external remote which might not have resilience to unsupported requests, while allowing for needed flexibility","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1518021681,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MzgzMDIzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363830239"},"message":"Doesn't the self.error make it crash?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518026752,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg1NzEzNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363857136"},"message":"I don't think so -- just reports to our log and sends ERROR message to parent git-annex.\nAlso it would make no sense then to `self.send` in the next line, would it? ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1518026843,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg1NzY0Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363857646"},"message":"Well, if it sends ERROR to git-annex, git-annex will then stop talking to it entirely, which is just as bad as the backtrace I was assuming.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518027371,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg2MDQ5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363860496"},"message":"oh... indeed.I should analyze our use of `self.error` then -- probably I should come up with a `.warning` which would send an `INFO` to annex with `WARNING: `-prefixed message, unless you see it worthwhile adding `WARNING` into special remote protocol.\nthanks for the note","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1518028016,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg2MzcwNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363863704"},"message":"git-annex deals with UNSUPPORTED-REQUEST on its own so you should not need to send back any INFO or do anything except send that.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1518030800,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg3NzgwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363877809"},"message":"Check out git-annex's new EXTENSIONS branch to see what happens when git-annex sends some unsupported request..","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518031071,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg3OTI5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363879293"},"message":"d'oh -- apparently I have dealt with this one  awhile back in 9d58db6b67525b75ae1a79677a6fbf5e811a49a8 which is (`0.9.1~5^2~3`) and thus current code is not like in original quote (I guess taken prior 0.9.1):\n```python\n            method = getattr(self, \"req_%s\" % req, None)\n            if not method:\n                self.debug(\"We have no support for %s request, part of %s response\"\n                           % (req, l))\n                self.send(\"UNSUPPORTED-REQUEST\")\n                continue\n```\nso we are Ok'ish.  But there are other places where we use `self.error` where we might need to reconsider.  I will close this issue pushing some minor tune ups on that end","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1518034061,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg5NDI3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363894274"},"message":"Ah ok, and current versions of git-annex send EXPORTSUPPORTED which triggers the same problem code in old datalad. But, that's done only if the datalad remote is configured for export, which I think it will never be, so luckily we avoided breaking it.\n\nRemains the question of what to do about the old versions of datalad that would be broken if I merge the EXTENSIONS branch into git-annex. Could make the git-annex package conflict with them or something..","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518034371,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mzg5NTY3MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-363895671"},"message":"IMHO that would be ok to demand datalad \u003e=0.9.1 ;-). At least on neuroDebians we assure to have datalad compatible with available through apt git annex","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520183178,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDI0NTM2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124#issuecomment-370245360"},"message":"was fixed in #2125","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520183179,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUwMjk5NTMzOA=="},"status":2}]}